  "_readme": [
    "Which tenders are kept, and which category each goes under.",
    "Edit the word lists below; no code change is needed. Matching ignores upper/lower case.",
    "1. evGateTerms: an EV-charging tender is kept only if its title contains at least one of these.",
    "2. categories: a kept EV tender is tagged with every category that has a matching phrase.",
    "   The FIRST matching category (in the order listed here) is the one shown on its card.",
    "   Phrases are regular expressions, so '.*' means 'anything in between'.",
    "3. fallbackCategory: used when a tender passes step 1 but matches no category.",
    "4. extraCategories: other products to keep even without an EV word (batteries, BESS,",
    "   power electronics...). A title matching one of these phrases is kept under that",
    "   category. Keep these phrases specific: '\\\\b' marks a word boundary, and '(?!...)'",
    "   excludes look-alikes (e.g. 'inverter' but not 'inverter split AC').",
    "After editing, run `python -m pytest` to check nothing broke."
